re flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Broadstone Net Lease, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.5B market cap on $454M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $270M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 15.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Real Estate peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","c